Experiment 1(a): Create and Attach an EBS Volume to an EC2 Instance
Aim

To create an Amazon EBS volume and attach it to an existing EC2 instance for additional storage.

Procedure
Step 1: Open EC2 Dashboard
Login to Amazon Web Services AWS Management Console.
Open EC2 Dashboard.
In the left menu select:
Elastic Block Store → Volumes
Step 2: Create New EBS Volume
Click Create Volume.
Configure:
Volume Type: gp3
Size: 10 GB (or required size)
Availability Zone: Same AZ as EC2 instance
Click Create Volume.
Step 3: Attach Volume to EC2 Instance
Select newly created volume.
Click:
Actions → Attach Volume
Select target EC2 instance.

Enter device name:

/dev/xvdf
Click Attach Volume.
Step 4: Connect to EC2 Instance

Use SSH:

ssh -i key.pem ec2-user@public-ip
Step 5: Verify Attached Volume

Run:

lsblk

You should see newly attached disk.

Observation
EBS volume created successfully.
Volume attached to EC2 instance.
New block storage device visible using lsblk.
Result

Successfully created and attached an EBS volume to the EC2 instance.
